('127.170.d.1.A',3,'A podcast producer proofreads show notes before publishing them. This applies:','["English language arts skills to audio work", "Plumbing skills", "Culinary skills", "Welding skills"]'::jsonb,0,'ELA in audio.','original'),
('127.170.d.1.A',4,'Writing a clear client email that states the session date, rate, and deliverables shows strong:','["Mixing speed", "Written communication", "Mic placement", "Cable wrapping"]'::jsonb,1,'ELA.','original'),
('127.170.d.1.B',3,'An engineer bills $90 per hour for 7 hours of mixing. What is the invoice amount?','["$560", "$700", "$630", "$97"]'::jsonb,2,'90 x 7 = 630.','original'),
('127.170.d.1.B',4,'A session runs from 1:15 p.m. to 6:45 p.m. How many hours long is it?','["5 hours", "4.5 hours", "6 hours", "5.5 hours"]'::jsonb,3,'5 hours 30 minutes = 5.5 hours.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.A',3,'Describing compression to a new singer without technical terms is adjusting language to the:','["Listener''s level of experience", "Length of the cable", "Color of the walls", "Brand of the mic"]'::jsonb,0,'Adapt language.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.A',4,'An email to a radio station manager is more formal in structure and style than a text to a bandmate because of the:','["Font size", "Audience and situation", "Battery life", "Screen color"]'::jsonb,1,'Adapt language.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.B',3,'Sorting recorded takes into folders for vocals, guitars, and drums is:','["Panning", "Over-compressing", "Organizing information", "Clipping"]'::jsonb,2,'Organize information.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.B',4,'Before presenting a mix plan to a client, a producer arranges the points in:','["Reverse alphabetical order only", "Random order", "No order", "A logical order"]'::jsonb,3,'Organize.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.C',3,'An engineer reads a spectrum analyzer and tells the artist the vocal has too much low-end rumble. This is:','["Interpreting and communicating data", "Wiring a lamp", "Painting a wall", "Booking a tour"]'::jsonb,0,'Interpret information.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.C',4,'A loudness meter reads well above the streaming target. A clear report to the client is:','["The meter is decorative", "The mix is louder than the platform target and needs adjusting", "The mix is perfect", "Loudness does not matter"]'::jsonb,1,'Communicate observations.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.D',3,'Walking a label executive through a finished album mix in a scheduled meeting is a:','["Break time", "Casual hallway chat", "Formal presentation", "Sound check joke"]'::jsonb,2,'Formal presentation.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.D',4,'Telling the band at the console what changed in the last take is a(n):','["Press release", "Keynote address", "Awards speech", "Informal presentation"]'::jsonb,3,'Informal presentation.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.E',3,'An engineer pauses, nods, and asks a follow-up question while a producer describes a vision. This is:','["Active listening", "Distracted listening", "Interrupting", "Ignoring"]'::jsonb,0,'Active listening.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.E',4,'Restating a client''s notes in your own words before editing helps ensure:','["The client leaves", "You understood the request", "The notes are ignored", "The deadline passes"]'::jsonb,1,'Active listening.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.F',3,'Recording a podcast guest who speaks with a strong regional accent calls for:','["Correcting every word", "Cutting them off", "Patience and respect", "Mockery"]'::jsonb,2,'Diverse individuals.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.F',4,'A team that includes musicians from many backgrounds is likely to produce:','["Fewer ideas", "Identical sounds", "More conflict only", "A wider range of creative ideas"]'::jsonb,3,'Diversity.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.G',3,'Sending a thank-you note and a prompt revised mix to a client builds the studio''s:','["Public relations and reputation", "Latency", "Gain structure", "Noise floor"]'::jsonb,0,'PR skills.','original'),
('127.170.d.2.G',4,'A studio gets a complaint about a late delivery. A strong public relations response is to:','["Delete the project", "Apologize, explain, and offer a firm new date", "Blame the client", "Ignore the message"]'::jsonb,1,'PR.','original'),
('127.170.d.3.A',3,'A producer tests three vocal chains and keeps the one that sounds best in the mix. This is:','["Flipping a coin", "Guessing", "Critical thinking", "Copying a rival"]'::jsonb,2,'Critical thinking.','original'),
('127.170.d.3.A',4,'A group evaluating two mastering quotes compares price, turnaround, and past work before deciding. This is:','["Random choice", "Avoidance", "Impulse buying", "Critical thinking as a team"]'::jsonb,3,'Critical thinking in groups.','original'),
('127.170.d.3.B',3,'Two engineers disagree on how much reverb a vocal needs. A good group solution is to:','["A/B both versions and listen together", "Let one person overrule without listening", "Walk away", "Argue louder"]'::jsonb,0,'Interpersonal skills.','original'),
('127.170.d.3.B',4,'An effective interpersonal approach to a team disagreement about the schedule is to:','["Assign blame", "Listen, compare needs, and reach a compromise", "Stay silent", "Pick sides"]'::jsonb,1,'Group problem solving.','original'),
('127.170.d.4.A',3,'Posting a behind-the-scenes clip to social media to promote a studio is:','["A safety rule", "A cable", "A technology application for marketing", "A hand tool"]'::jsonb,2,'Technology applications.','original'),
('127.170.d.4.A',4,'Using a word processor to prepare a session contract and email to send it is an example of:','["Mixing in analog", "Tape editing", "Soldering", "Using writing and communication software"]'::jsonb,3,'Technology applications.','original'),
('127.170.d.4.B',3,'Naming files with a clear pattern such as project, date, and version is:','["File management", "Mastering", "Equalization", "Compression"]'::jsonb,0,'File management.','original'),
('127.170.d.4.B',4,'Keeping client contacts, notes, and deadlines in one secure system is:','["Hiding data", "Personal information management", "Duplicating files", "Wasting memory"]'::jsonb,1,'Information management.','original'),
('127.170.d.5.A',3,'Moving from phonograph records to magnetic tape to digital audio workstations shows the:','["End of sound", "Decline of music", "Evolution of the audio production industry", "Birth of silent film"]'::jsonb,2,'History of audio.','original'),
('127.170.d.5.A',4,'The introduction of the compact disc in the 1980s moved consumers toward:','["Telegraph signals", "Silent media", "Wax cylinders", "Digital music formats"]'::jsonb,3,'History of audio.','original'),
('127.170.d.5.B',3,'The rise of podcasts and streaming playlists is a current trend that:','["Creates demand for new audio content", "Eliminates audio jobs", "Ends recording", "Bans music"]'::jsonb,0,'Current trends.','original'),
('127.170.d.5.B',4,'A producer analyzing trends notices more listeners using earbuds on phones. A smart response is to:','["Ignore small speakers", "Check mixes on small consumer devices", "Remove all bass", "Mix only for large rooms"]'::jsonb,1,'Analyze trends.','original'),
('127.170.d.6.A',3,'Using a lift technique or a helper to move a heavy speaker cabinet is:','["Optional", "Slowing work down", "Following workplace safety rules", "A style choice"]'::jsonb,2,'Safety rules.','original'),
('127.170.d.6.A',4,'Safe studio cable management means:','["Stretching cords across doorways", "Leaving cables tangled", "Stacking cords near water", "Routing cords away from walkways"]'::jsonb,3,'Safety regulations.','original'),
('127.170.d.6.B',3,'During a power outage in the studio, the engineer should first:','["Move calmly to safety and follow emergency steps", "Run toward the stage", "Keep recording", "Open every equipment case"]'::jsonb,0,'Emergency procedures.','original'),
('127.170.d.6.B',4,'A fire extinguisher in the control room should be:','["Hidden behind gear", "Clearly marked and easy to reach", "Locked away", "Removed"]'::jsonb,1,'Emergency procedures.','original'),
('127.170.d.7.A',3,'A senior student who assigns roles for a recording day and keeps the group focused is showing:','["Disorganization", "Indifference", "Leadership skills", "Avoidance"]'::jsonb,2,'Leadership.','original'),
('127.170.d.7.A',4,'A strong leader on a project responds to a mistake by:','["Blaming a teammate", "Quitting", "Hiding it", "Taking responsibility and fixing the problem"]'::jsonb,3,'Leadership.','original'),
('127.170.d.7.B',3,'Sharing credit for a finished mix with the whole team shows:','["Teamwork", "Selfishness", "Rivalry", "Isolation"]'::jsonb,0,'Teamwork.','original'),
('127.170.d.7.B',4,'A good first step to manage a conflict between two crew members is to:','["Ignore it", "Let each person explain their side", "Take sides", "Raise your voice"]'::jsonb,1,'Conflict management.','original'),
('127.170.d.7.C',3,'In a planning meeting, a team member helps most by:','["Leaving early", "Texting", "Staying on topic and offering ideas", "Interrupting"]'::jsonb,2,'Meetings.','original'),
('127.170.d.7.C',4,'Sending meeting minutes afterward ensures that the team:','["Doubles work", "Forgets tasks", "Misses deadlines", "Remembers its decisions and next tasks"]'::jsonb,3,'Meetings.','original'),
('127.170.d.7.D',3,'An alumnus who volunteers to review a student''s demo reel is:','["Mentoring", "Ignoring", "Competing", "Delaying"]'::jsonb,0,'Mentoring.','original'),
('127.170.d.7.D',4,'Taking part in a mentoring program helps a student by:','["Limiting contacts", "Providing guidance on skills and career steps", "Reducing options", "Blocking feedback"]'::jsonb,1,'Mentoring.','original'),
('127.170.d.8.A',3,'Telling a client honestly that a file is corrupted instead of hiding it is:','["A technical fault", "An accident", "Ethical conduct", "Poor planning"]'::jsonb,2,'Ethical conduct.','original'),
('127.170.d.8.A',4,'Respecting a talent''s privacy by not sharing their unreleased recordings is an example of:','["Optional courtesy", "Poor mixing", "Marketing", "Ethical professional behavior"]'::jsonb,3,'Ethical conduct.','original'),
('127.170.d.8.B',3,'Paying for a sample pack license instead of copying a competitor''s samples shows:','["Respect for intellectual property", "Wastefulness", "Carelessness", "Disregard for creators"]'::jsonb,0,'IP respect.','original'),
('127.170.d.8.B',4,'Crediting a session musician in the liner notes shows respect for their:','["Travel route", "Creative contribution", "Pay rate only", "Equipment"]'::jsonb,1,'IP respect.','original'),
('127.170.d.8.C',3,'Audio producers can shape public opinion because the work they release influences:','["Soil quality", "Road signs", "What people hear and believe", "The weather"]'::jsonb,2,'Ethical impact.','original'),
('127.170.d.8.C',4,'Using audio editing to make a political figure appear to say something they never said raises:','["A style choice", "No concern", "A technical bonus", "A serious ethical problem"]'::jsonb,3,'Ethical impact.','original'),
('127.170.d.8.D',3,'Copyright protects an original recording from being:','["Copied or sold without permission", "Recorded at all", "Talked about", "Heard by anyone"]'::jsonb,0,'Copyright.','original'),
